---
/**
 * How the listings are made, and what it would take to change one.
 *
 * This is the page local news sites, libraries and community groups link to,
 * and it is the thing that separates a guide from a scraped directory. It is
 * also the page to point at when a business asks why it cannot buy its way up
 * the list.
 */
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro';
import { getSite, liveTowns } from '@/config';

const site = getSite();
const what = site.kind === 'town' ? site.siteTitle : 'Every guide in the network';
const live = liveTowns();
---
<Page
  title="Editorial policy"
  eyebrow={site.kind === 'town' ? site.name : 'Inside the Towns'}
  description={`How listings on ${site.siteTitle} are researched, checked and corrected, and why nothing on it can be bought.`}
  intro="What goes on these pages, where it comes from, how often it is checked, and what to do when it is wrong."
  narrow
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Nothing here is paid for</h2>
    <p>
      Listings are free and editorial. No business pays to be listed, and no business can pay to be higher up a page
      or to be marked as a pick. If sponsorship ever appears on these sites it will be labeled as sponsorship and it
      will sit beside the listings, never inside them.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the facts come from</h2>
    <p>
      {what} takes its facts from the operator’s own page first: a restaurant’s own site for its hours, a town’s own
      calendar for a council meeting, an organizer’s own listing for a festival. Where a business has no site, or a
      site with no hours, the listing simply has none. A guess that looks like a fact is worse than a gap.
    </p>
    <p>
      Review sites and business-listing directories are not used as sources. Their hours are user-editable and
      frequently stale, and their photographs are not ours to publish.
    </p>

    <h2>Everything carries its date</h2>
    <p>
      Every place and every event records the source it was read from and the day it was last checked against that
      source, and both are shown on the listing. A weekly report flags anything that has gone ninety days without a
      re-check. Hours go stale faster than anything else on these sites, so the operator’s own page is always the
      record and the listing is a pointer to it.
    </p>

    <h2>Events</h2>
    <p>
      No event is listed without a source. Dates are checked against the weekday they claim to fall on, which is what
      catches a page that is quietly last year’s. A recurring event is stored as one entry per occurrence, so what you
      see is the date it actually happens rather than a rule you have to apply yourself. Past events drop off on their
      own.
    </p>

    <h2>Photographs</h2>
    <p>
      Every photograph on these sites is public domain, openly licensed, taken by us, or published with the owner’s
      written permission — and every one is recorded with its source, its terms and whether credit is required.
      Credit is shown wherever the license or the owner asks for it; a photograph whose record says credit is
      required and whose page does not show one fails the build. Businesses’ own marketing photographs, and
      photographs from review sites, are not used.
    </p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>
      {site.kind === 'town' ? `${site.siteTitle} is` : 'None of these guides is'} a government site, a chamber of
      commerce or any public body, and {site.kind === 'town' ? 'it does' : 'they do'} not speak for one. Anything
      civic links out to the official source rather than being paraphrased here.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is wrong, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> and it will be fixed, usually within a day or two.
      Corrections are made quietly to listings, because a wrong phone number does not need a public notice; a
      correction to an article is noted on the article. There is no appeal process for being left out and no payment
      that changes it — if a place belongs in a guide, say so and it goes in.
    </p>

    {site.kind === 'hub' && (
      <p>
        This policy applies to all {live.length} guides: {live.map((t) => t.siteTitle).join(', ')}.
      </p>
    )}
  </div>
</Page>
